kqr0-6KKVwrW3YT_Cg8CdWGTW8crmtj1-WpjbW3fCgNr1SCS2gW7mlytn5mtftSW92P99P3X4PF=
NW5W7FpM6DF8_XW6zPDJW32xf8PW5k9tb853RpHTW7lq64H3kFwB6W5CNy_F6LqFZQW4lSlbb2c=
d9yqN3Zj0VLT-RTHW10_pqH4vjwkXf72vYyP04" style=3D"color:#192733" data-hs-lin=
k-id=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"QOQo5dKN" target=3D"_blank">per</a> <span =
style=3D"font-style: italic;">The Washington Post.</span></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:115%; font-weight:bold; font-size:18px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:115%; font-size:18px"><strong>How they work&nbsp;</=
strong></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><br>These apps help minors learn about financ=
ial literacy through educational videos and gamified lessons, and by giving=
 them debit cards and access to manage their own funds. Teens with jobs can=
 receive direct deposits through their accounts.&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; font-weight:bold; font-size:22px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Parents, meanwhile, can automate allowances, =
pay their kids for completing chores, receive real-time notifications about=
 transactions, set spending limits, and block certain vendors.&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; font-weight:bold; font-size:22px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Most offer a free tier, with monthly subscrip=
tions usually starting at ~$5 and increasing from there, depending on add-o=
ns, like cash back rewards.&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; font-weight:bold; font-size:22px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><span style=3D"font-size: 18px;"><strong>One =
popular family money app=E2=80=A6&nbsp;</strong></span></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; font-weight:bold; font-size:22px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">=E2=80=A6 is Greenlight, which boasts 6.5m+ u=
sers, 4m+ of whom have joined in the last five years.&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; font-weight:bold; font-size:22px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">In 2024, kids and teens managed a record $2B =
through its app, according to the company=E2=80=99s <a href=3D"https://medi=
a.hubspot.com/e3t/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VWLGc76WG5HSW3gS-Xy8S2HpxW7bJF9w5FTcH=
fM_h9pn2-ZW0W6N1vHY6lZ3kqV5DVjz2CD08gVw3Pn16KJWpcW1g_10s2bnf7zW1HL9k-1NWJG0=
W56843l4JGRR8W5vplmB28Vvx1W7NbsnB6SK3VMVfHClY700vWsW8FNxfS6SFHh9W6l_9rS2hHz=
nHW8_XrJB5_PGwxW84DTtt66JS8-W5M-Mw04KFspzW9hDVTq3XNgTpW590cD_1mML6NW7XFFVK5=
4VRB8W2XY3G31s7301W3JsC-l1WWYlGW5scy7Y1LRcgpW60y5d_22CBbhW5T6DbJ3-vmnDW1FRT=
yj4y06GHf7QqNBl04" style=3D"color:#192733" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-li=
nk-id-v2=3D"thFsS3Ep" target=3D"_blank">annual report</a>, which also found=
:</p>
<ul style=3D"line-height:150%">
<li aria-level=3D"1">The average allowance across age groups was $13.42.<br=
><br></li>
<li aria-level=3D"1">Their monthly spend hovered at $126, with much of it g=
oing to companies like Amazon and DoorDash.<br><br></li>
<li aria-level=3D"1">Collectively, they stashed away $259m, with most savin=
g toward cars, college, and their futures, and invested $43m into stocks li=
ke Apple and Nvidia.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Other platforms include Acorns Early (<a href=
=3D"https://media.hubspot.com/e3t/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VWLGc76WG5HSW3gS-Xy8S=
2HpxW7bJF9w5FTcHfM_h9p44ZwpbW69t95C6lZ3pHW8BY-Bm1JcGw6N42vTbJbqxBsW5Wv-3r3Z=
Q9DyW2Xmkv73PCGvlVyV7z66YnxGVW57XTHT3zSq--W5wZTGL1FsrrfW6VyFyc6sQSx_W4kt_qf=
4QQdcHW27H9VN52ZCRBN7Rbx-RRQvYGW4XJjVZ325fZdW1gGKW_6_rzcXW1djcNX5ZpzQ-W1RlS=
rX6TtsRHW6C5-8s8RFnc8W50pt4C3hhc8zW5r90Ll8CG4J6W2w_gfl2YNK9TVQQhQX2vStTTW82=
SbDx7yTry7W6kxz6Q7sRT_-W78hsvj2S1dCZW3t1BPP3JwPWJW4KC6ll8sFCTmW2pBc0s6tfrjv=
W83D7n96KvHQ_W5rN9wl6hX-vNW4jfP3R4q6_0qW537rL95PHfKCW92sl_h4JhYw3W41wW_R6r8=
_DZW4lK4HH7XxwSxW9kB1gl25FvX3W5rXr6s7y5XhlN1QR1-GTY3LVf8xkBvj04" style=3D"c=
olor:#192733" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"X+GifJJ+" target=
=3D"_blank">3.3m</a> global users), as well as Jassby, Kachinga, FamZoo, an=
d Modak.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; font-weight:bold; font-size:22px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><span style=3D"font-size: 18px;"><strong>Bank=
 or bust?</strong></span></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; font-weight:bold; font-size:22px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">While it frankly feels wrong for a child to k=
now anything about Nvidia, these apps set them up with key skills that many=
 of us missed out on.</p>
<ul style=3D"line-height:150%">
<li aria-level=3D"1">The financial literacy rate is just <a href=3D"https:/=
/media.hubspot.com/e3t/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VWLGc76WG5HSW3gS-Xy8S2HpxW7bJF9w=
5FTcHfM_h9p42-ZW0W69sMD-6lZ3kDMfTw8xdw2MrW2LhsjJ7Cm6t3W7sd5Bj4qsNNXW7L9-r05=
GbqmqW2mNC3F9b0zhBVy8KKR7R9jRsW3w0SRd32WfH5W2s63V56HWWzTW20Xbsp3gQDVBW2gHRN=
G4FVhv8W5D4JdN40xsBFVGV6xv1f6XyYW4nHCsv3STMZpW6cNfJn6ft8NsW4kfQn494gdrSW1VT=
Sl55SXC0FVTqscY2csKtfW4SDydX1DkDkYW5Krcbk5fhV3DW3KhXYl3SQtVmf61l5PW04" styl=
e=3D"color:#192733" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"uWpafCRb" t=
arget=3D"_blank">57%</a> in the US, and even lower globally (33%).</li>
</ul>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Mixing minors with sensitive personal informa=
tion does, however, raise obvious privacy concerns, like media-illiterate t=
ots=E2=80=99 vulnerability to scams and hacks, and what the companies might=
 do with their data.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><br>Despite the risks, parents who spoke to <=
em>The Post</em> said the apps have helped their kids learn important lesso=
ns about money and, in some cases, even give them a sense of financial empo=
werment. &nbsp; <br><br>One Acorns user reportedly told her mother, =E2=80=
=9CSpending your own money feels so much better than when somebody buys it =
for you.=E2=80=9D<br><br>Yeah, that=E2=80=99ll change.<br><br></p>
